      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common reasons include blocked air return vents in that bedroom or temporary duct insulation issues. A collapsed or disconnected duct in the supply line to that specific room can also prevent airflow. Additionally, the thermostat might be miscalibrated or located in a spot that doesn't accurately reflect the thermostat's intended location, leading to off-balancing.",
