    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the vents and they aren't blocked by furniture or anything. could it be something hidden inside the walls or ceiling? like maybe something's actually damaging the ducts or something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, hidden issues inside the wall cavities or ceiling are very common culprits, such as wet insulation or construction debris causing a duct to collapse or restrict airflow. If the duct is severely crushed or disconnected behind those walls, you might need to reset the circuit breaker for that zone or a thermostat. Without specialized vacuum gage equipment, you may not be able to diagnose the exact blockage, so professional HVAC technicians are usually necessary for this level of inspection.",
